Package: optithresholdr
Title: Data-Driven Thresholds for Wearable Time-in-Range Summaries
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Junyoung", "Park", email = "junyoup@umich.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Neo", "Kok", email = "irinagn@umich.edu", role = "aut"),
    person("Irina", "Gaynanova", email = "irinagn@umich.edu", role = "aut"),
    person("Farhad", "De Sousa", email = "fdesousa@usc.edu", role = "ctb"))
Author: Junyoung Park [aut, cre], Neo Kok [aut], Irina Gaynanova [aut], Farhad De Sousa [ctb]
Maintainer: Junyoung Park <junyoup@umich.edu>
Description: Implements mathematically grounded threshold selection for
    time-in-range summaries of repeated wearable measurements such as
    continuous glucose monitor data. The package uses the full measurement
    profiles across subjects to estimate cutoffs that optimally preserve
    distributional information in the resulting summaries, using
    Wasserstein-based loss functions and differential evolution.
